.TH D_TUFT 1 "February 2026" "d_tuft 1.0" "EVM Bytecode Toolkit"
.SH NAME
d_tuft \- bidirectional EVM bytecode ↔ opcode transformer and analysis toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B d_tuft
[\-\-help] [\-\-version]
.I <command>
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
d_tuft provides CLI tools for disassembling, assembling, comparing, and analyzing Ethereum smart contract bytecode and opcodes. It supports round-trip testing, function identification, and multiple output formats.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS disasm (alias: d)
Disassemble EVM bytecode to readable opcodes.
.RS
.TP
\fBUsage:\fR
.B d_tuft disasm <input> [\fIoptions\fR]
.TP
\fBArguments:\fR
.I <input>\: Input bytecode file (hex string or file path)
.TP
\fBOptions:\fR
\fB\-o, \-\-output <file>\fR\: Output file (defaults to stdout)
\fB\-f, \-\-format <format>\fR\: Output format: text, annotated, json (default: text)
\fB\-\-no\-pc\fR\: Omit program counter
\fB\-\-gas\fR\: Include gas costs in output
\fB\-\-hex\fR\: Include hex bytes
.RE
.SS asm (alias: a)
Assemble opcodes to bytecode.
.RS
.TP
\fBUsage:\fR
.B d_tuft asm <input> [\fIoptions\fR]
.TP
\fBArguments:\fR
.I <input>\: Input assembly file
.TP
\fBOptions:\fR
\fB\-o, \-\-output <file>\fR\: Output file (default: stdout)
.RE
.SS compare (alias: c)
Compare two bytecode or assembly files for equivalence.
.RS
.TP
\fBUsage:\fR
.B d_tuft compare <file1> <file2> [\fIoptions\fR]
.TP
\fBArguments:\fR
.I <file1>\: First input file (bytecode or assembly)
.I <file2>\: Second input file (bytecode or assembly)
.TP
\fBOptions:\fR
\fB\-\-format <format>\fR\: Input format: auto, bytecode, assembly (default: auto)
.RE
.SS test
Test round-trip bytecode → opcodes → bytecode fidelity.
.RS
.TP
\fBUsage:\fR
.B d_tuft test <input>
.TP
\fBArguments:\fR
.I <input>\: Input bytecode (hex string or file)
.RE
.SS identify (alias: id)
Identify functions in bytecode and analyze contract structure.
.RS
.TP
\fBUsage:\fR
.B d_tuft identify <input> [\fIoptions\fR]
.TP
\fBArguments:\fR
.I <input>\: Input bytecode (hex string or file) or assembly file
.TP
\fBOptions:\fR
\fB\-\-format <format>\fR\: Output format: text, annotated, json (default: text)
\fB\-\-abi <file>\fR\: ABI JSON file for resolving function names
\fB\-o, \-\-output <file>\fR\: Output file (defaults to stdout)
\fB\-\-internal\fR\: Also list internal/private functions (orphan JUMPDESTs)
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Disassemble bytecode:
.IP
.nf
\fIUnix/macOS:\fR
$ bun run src/cli/index.ts disasm examples/contract.bin -o output.evm

\fIWindows:\fR
> bun run src/cli/index.ts disasm examples\\contract.bin -o output.evm
.fi

Identify functions with ABI:
.IP
.nf
\fIUnix/macOS:\fR
$ bun run src/cli/index.ts identify contract.bin --abi contract.abi --format annotated

\fIWindows:\fR
> bun run src/cli/index.ts identify contract.bin --abi contract.abi --format annotated
.fi

Compare two contracts:
.IP
.nf
\fIUnix/macOS:\fR
$ bun run src/cli/index.ts compare contract1.evm contract2.evm

\fIWindows:\fR
> bun run src/cli/index.ts compare contract1.evm contract2.evm
.fi

.SH PLATFORM NOTES
.SS Unix/macOS
Use standard path separators (/). Commands can be chained with pipes.
.SS Windows
Use backslashes (\\) in paths or quote paths with spaces. PowerShell and CMD support the same command syntax. On Windows, you may need to use quotes around paths with backslashes:
.IP
.nf
> bun run src/cli/index.ts disasm "C:\\path\\to\\contract.bin"
.fi

.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
.TP
\fBtext\fR
Human-readable format with optional PC, gas, and hex byte annotations.
.TP
\fBannotated\fR
Detailed format with box-drawing characters, gas costs, and full instruction details.
.TP
\fBjson\fR
Machine-readable JSON output for programmatic processing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success
.TP
1
Error (invalid input, mismatch, or operation failure)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR evm (1),
.BR solc (1)
